Here's a simple HTML and JavaScript example to create an interactive joke website:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .container {
            text-align: center;
            background: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 2px solid #007BFF;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .joke {
            margin: 20px 0;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            color: #333;
        }
        .reveal {
            display: none;
            color: #007BFF;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke">
            <p>[Funny Joke]</p>
            <p class="reveal">[push to reveal punchline]</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        document.querySelector('.reveal').addEventListener('click', function() {
            const joke = document.querySelector('.joke');
            joke.innerHTML = `
                <p>Why don't scientists trust atoms?</p>
                <p>Because they make up everything!</p>
            `;
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple webpage with a joke that is revealed when the user clicks on the "push to reveal punchline" text. The design includes some basic styling for a colorful and interactive look.
